--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+Fizzy creates one delivery for each active webhook subscribed to an event. Each delivery is POSTed once and is de-duplicated by event and webhook. Successful HTTP responses have a `2XX` status; all other responses and connection errors are recorded as failures. Ten consecutive failures whose first failure occurred within the previous hour automatically deactivate the receiver. A successful delivery resets the failure streak, and reactivating a webhook starts a new streak.
+
+Requests use `Content-Type: application/json`. `X-Webhook-Timestamp` contains the event's UTC ISO 8601 timestamp, and `X-Webhook-Signature` contains an HMAC-SHA256 digest of the exact request body using the webhook's signing secret. Generic receivers get the event JSON shown by the event payload template; Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp chat receivers get their native `text` or `content` payload.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
@@ -64,7 +68,7 @@ __Request:__
 ```
 
 `subscribed_actions` accepts any of:
-`card_assigned`, `card_closed`, `card_postponed`, `card_auto_postponed`, `card_board_changed`, `card_published`, `card_reopened`, `card_sent_back_to_triage`, `card_triaged`, `card_unassigned`, `comment_created`
+`card_assigned`, `card_closed`, `card_postponed`, `card_auto_postponed`, `card_board_changed`, `card_published`, `card_reopened`, `card_title_changed`, `card_sent_back_to_triage`, `card_triaged`, `card_unassigned`, `comment_created`
 
 __Response:__
 
@@ -159,3 +163,5 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
